{
  "an11.4:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 11.4 ",
  "an11.4:0.2": "1. Dependence ",
  "an11.4:0.3": "Vital Conditions (2nd) ",
  "an11.4:1.1": "There Venerable Sāriputta addressed the mendicants: ",
  "an11.4:1.2": "“Reverends, mendicants!” ",
  "an11.4:1.3": "“Reverend,” they replied. ",
  "an11.4:1.4": "Sāriputta said this: ",
  "an11.4:2.1": "“An unethical person, who lacks ethics, has destroyed a vital condition for not having regrets. ",
  "an11.4:2.2": "When there are regrets, one who has regrets has destroyed a vital condition for joy. ",
  "an11.4:2.3": "When there is no joy, one who lacks joy has destroyed a vital condition for rapture. ",
  "an11.4:2.4": "When there is no rapture, one who lacks rapture has destroyed a vital condition for tranquility. ",
  "an11.4:2.5": "When there is no tranquility, one who lacks tranquility has destroyed a vital condition for bliss. ",
  "an11.4:2.6": "When there is no bliss, one who lacks bliss has destroyed a vital condition for right immersion. ",
  "an11.4:2.7": "When there is no right immersion, one who lacks right immersion has destroyed a vital condition for true knowledge and vision. ",
  "an11.4:2.8": "When there is no true knowledge and vision, one who lacks true knowledge and vision has destroyed a vital condition for disillusionment. ",
  "an11.4:2.9": "When there is no disillusionment, one who lacks disillusionment has destroyed a vital condition for dispassion. ",
  "an11.4:2.10": "When there is no dispassion, one who lacks dispassion has destr